/T (Nigeria stands at a pivotal civic moment. Voter turnout  has fallen to a historic low of 27%, civic space has been  formally classified as Repressed by international  monitors, and a funding crisis has destabilised the civil  society infrastructure that was filling the gaps left by  government institutions. Yet the signals are not uniformly  negative. As of April 2026, over 3.7 million Nigerians  have registered for 2027, 68% of them youth. INEC itself )
